From df9f8ce91032c14594e3a71c8fee0e82819481c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bvchess <53128914+bvchess@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:49:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Prover: force the members the parity bound certifies (exact
 --fix-certified 1)

upper::certify(board, spf, v, ustar, start, iterate) bars each member of U*_{>=3}
from the starting roles, certifies those whose parity bound is at most v (or
whose barring is infeasible), and with `iterate` forces them and bars the
members still open again, round after round until one certifies nothing.  It
returns the roles with the certified members forced, the rounds, and how many
members the first round certified.  barred_bounds is now its first round (the
loop exists once); upper's default output is byte-identical to the committed
data/upper_*.jsonl (checked on five games, all but secs).

exact --fix-certified 1 (off by default; needs --fix-low 1, refused with
--fix-upper 1) searches from the roles of F4 plus the forced members.  It is a
proof: a set beating V and obeying F4 holds every member certified against V,
and every round rests only on "every such set holds the members certified so
far".  The certificates are computed against the search's own target.  The
line stays "proven" and gains fix_certified, certified, members,
certify_rounds and certify_secs (0 for a game not searched); the checkpoint
kind is _cert and carries certify_secs.  tools/summarize.py exact and check
and prover.sh --verify count these lines as proofs without a change.
upper --iterate 1 writes the iterated certification (rounds, certified_first).

Tests: the enumerating harness over boards 2..60 at claims V-1, V-2 and V-5
now also checks the iterated certificates against every playable set obeying
F4 that beats the claim, the forced roles, and the iterated deliberately wrong
rule (caught on 12 boards).  A search from the forced roles proves V on games
432, 476 and 528 and, with the certificates computed against V - 1, finds a
set worth V.  exact: the refusals, and a line with the new fields on games 191,
216 and 432, with decoy checkpoints of other kinds left alone.

The parity bound is the exact maximum over the sets independent at both
parities, so the rounds after the first certify nothing: a heaviest set with
an open member barred that beats V holds every certified member.  The test
checks that the open members and their margins are unchanged by forcing.

Smoke (one thread each, release, a busy machine; games 1309, 1508, 1920):
  nodes with and without --fix-certified: 17887, 24078, 18887, the same
  seconds with, without: 85.7 / 85.2, 131.9 / 131.5, 134.1 / 132.5
  members 373, 436, 565; certified 368, 431, 554 after the first round and
  after the last; 2 rounds each; certify_secs 1.36, 1.75, 2.72
The search's own propagation already forces these members at its root, so the
forced roles give the same search.
